{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Transpose MIDI notes up or down to next visible note in Custom Note Order view (or just transpose notes by a semitone)\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Track Compass\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Inspired by LKC Tools Project Navigator, Track Compass allows you to focus on only the tracks you're working on without extra clutter. With Focus View on, only selected tracks get shown. With it off, you get a representation of your tracks, use it to select and navigate around. Regardless of what you do, Track Compass remembers the way you like your project set up. On startup, it takes as snapshot of your project, this means:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Archived or hidden tracks stay hidden\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab MIDI only tracks (with hidden MCPs) only get their TCP recalled\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FX return tracks (hidden in the arrange view) only get their MCP recalled If you add tracks later, press the * button (beside the ALL button), and a new snapshot is taken.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Other features:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Ctrl/Cmd click for multi-select\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Alt/Opt click or turn on Solo mode for soloing\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Adapts to your theme It's currently a work-in-progress, but the plan is to support a keyboard-centric (if desired), workflow, inspired by vim. And, of course, add some bells and whistles.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 (Current?) Limitations:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No click-and-drag to select\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No toggling folder states\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Requires taking another snapshot when new tracks are created\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Roadmap:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Auto add newly created tracks\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Option to not show hidden or MCP-only tracks in list\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Remember state when quit\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab expand/collapse folders\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Save snapshot with project\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab keyboard navigation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab allow drag-select\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab represent solo state in list\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab search + shortcuts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab represent track color in list\sa180\par}
}
